Assistant: Certainly. Suppose you want to mark a method as a test method in your unit testing framework, you can define an annotation like this:

```annotations
@interface Test {
    int value() default 0;
}
```

Then, you can use it like this:

```java
@Test
public void myTestMethod() {
    // your test code here
}
```

